-- Phase 3 of the NPC / bestiary work, fourth book: every species Rifts World Book
-- 15: Spirit West stats - its monsters (Black-Winged Monster-Men, Man-Eagles, the
-- three Man-Monsters, Plumed Serpents, Stone Giants, Teepowka, Two-Faced
-- Star-People, Ukt Water Serpents, the Wendigo), the three tribes of the Great
-- Little Ones, and its lesser and greater spirit TYPES - rows for creatures
-- (migration 074) and their attacks in stat_attacks (owner_kind 'creature').
--
-- One-off data script, run once per environment. NOT a migration.
--
-- NOT HERE: the named Great Spirits (the Four Kachina Godlings, Old Flame Dancing,
-- Ever Tide, Standing Mountain, Uktena, Whispering Maiden) and the gods (printed
-- 173-188) - they are individuals, for notable_npcs, and are not imported yet; the
-- Kachina Dancer, a role layered on a class; the totem animals, which are rules.
--
-- A RIFTS BOOK: an M.D.C. creature's pool is its M.D.C.; any S.D.C.-world figures
-- are in pools_note. The Wendigo is the one species the book offers as an optional
-- R.C.C.; it is also a published class. The three Man-Monsters are transformed
-- humans whose book stats are bonuses to a human's own attributes: each is stored
-- as 3D6 (a human's roll) plus the printed bonus, and the percentage reductions
-- and the M.D.C. carried over from the human's pools - which no formula can say -
-- are in pools_note.
--
-- EXTRACTED by four book-extract-workers, each given the NAMES of its species,
-- every number read off a 200 dpi render rather than the OCR cache, which carries
-- the digit cipher. RECONCILED by book-reconcile against the renders, row by row;
-- its corrections are applied. Every row passes creatureFormulaGaps, the grammar
-- the endpoint rolls with. description and natural_abilities are short
-- paraphrases - no sentence is the book's.
--
--   node scripts/d1-apply.mjs --local apps/character-creator/db/add-creatures-spirit-west.sql
--
-- BY CATEGORY:
--   monster (10): Black-Winged Monster-Men, Man-Eagles, Animal Man-Monster, Plant
--     Man-Monster, Spirit Man-Monster, Plumed Serpents, Teepowka, Two-Faced
--     Star-People, Ukt Water Serpents, Wendigo
--   faerie (3): Hunter Great Little Ones, Stone Thrower Great Little Ones, Nurturer
--     Great Little Ones
--   giant (1): Stone Giants
--   spirit (14): Lesser Animal Spirits, Lesser Plant Spirits, Lesser Elemental
--     Spirits, Kachina Tectonic Spirit, Lesser Kachina Spirit, Great Kachina Spirits,
--     Ondi Thunderbirds, Greater Air Spirit, Greater Earth Spirit, Greater Fire
--     Spirit, Greater Water Spirit, Greater Totem Animal Spirits, Tree Spirits,
--     Nunnehi

INSERT INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'black-winged-monster-men', 'Black-Winged Monster-Men', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Any evil; less than 5% anarchist', '{"IQ":"3D6","ME":"3D6","MA":"2D6","PS":"15+3D6","PP":"3D6+4","PE":"3D6+6","PB":"1D6","Spd":"3D6"}', NULL, NULL, '1D4x100', '2D4x10', NULL, 'All physical attributes are supernatural. Spd is 3D6x10 in flight. Each wing has its own 80+1D6x10 M.D.C.', NULL, 15, '{"attacks":6,"initiative":1,"strike":2,"parry":3,"dodge":1,"roll":2,"pull":3}', '+2 vs poison and magic; +6 save vs horror factor. Vulnerable to cold iron: contact gives -1 to all rolls; iron chains can leave it dazed/stunned (save vs non-lethal poison, then -4 strike/parry/dodge and -15% skills for 1D4 minutes). Weapons of cold iron do double their normal S.D.C. damage in M.D.; dodge: +1 on ground, +3 in flight', 'Basic math, land navigation, track humanoids, intelligence, interrogation, prowl, and climb, all at +20%. Plus two W.P.s of choice (prefers natural claws/powers); speaks Dragonese, Gobbledy, and Demongogian at 94%.', 'Nightvision 600 ft; winged flight; impervious to lightning/electricity; can repel animals at will with no P.P.E. cost; heals at twice normal rate; unaffected by sunlight; fires lightning bolts from hands and mouth.', 'Rare (about 1 in 400): a 1D6th level Ley Line Walker or Necromancer, never higher than 6th level', NULL, '12-20 ft tall (3.6-6 m); wingspan three times height', '500-1,000 lbs (225-450 kg)', 'About 500 years', 'Ruins of cities and mountains', 'human sorcerers and Shamans (occasionally)', 'Cyber-Knights; Sky-Knights; wild Psi-Stalkers (in the north); the Nez Perce of the Nimipu Preserve; heroes and champions of good in general', NULL, 'Demonic bat-winged giants who enslaved humans in a ruined pre-Rifts city, now warring with the Nez Perce over Idaho''s Nimipu Preserve.', 'Rifts World Book 15: Spirit West p.106-107');
INSERT INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'man-eagles', 'Man-Eagles', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Any evil, but 55% are aberrant; some are open to armed contests to win the return of kidnapped women', '{"IQ":"3D6","ME":"3D6","MA":"2D6","PS":"4D6","PP":"4D6","PE":"6D6","PB":"1D6","Spd":"3D6"}', NULL, NULL, '6D6+PE', '5D6+PE', NULL, 'All physical attributes are supernatural. Spd is 3D4x10 in flight. M.D.C. gains an additional 2D6 per level of experience. Wings: 45+1D4x10 M.D.C. each. Flint armor: 100 M.D.C., immune to fire/heat including magic fire and M.D.C. plasma/heat; repairs at 1 point per P.P.E. spent (recovered normally), needs a minute of concentration, cannot be done in combat.', NULL, 12, '{"attacks":5,"initiative":4,"strike":2,"parry":2,"disarm":1,"dodge":4,"roll":3,"pull":2}', 'Five physical attacks or two magic attacks per melee round. +2 save vs poison and magic; +6 save vs horror factor. Vulnerable to fire: normal fire does M.D., a torch strike does 4D6 M.D., magical/mega-damage fire does double damage.; dodge: +4 in flight', 'Basic math 80%, land navigation 98%, astronomy 90%, wilderness survival 90%, track humanoids 88%, intelligence 85%, interrogation 80%, prowl 80%, climb 95/90%, acrobatics 90%, sing 90%. Plus three W.P.s of choice (love magic weapons but rely on natural claws/powers); speaks all traditional Indian languages, Dragonese, and Demongogian at 95%.', 'Heightened hearing; flight up to 175 mph (280 kph); Sixth Sense identical to the psionic power but constantly active with no I.S.P. cost; can turn into mist at will, drifting at a sluggish speed or riding the wind.', 'Natural elemental abilities limited to globe of daylight, thunderclap, float in air, and escape', NULL, '7-9 ft tall (2.1-2.7 m); wingspan twice their height', '300-400 lbs (135-180 kg)', 'About 100 to 130 years', 'Prefers mountains and highlands; found throughout the New West and southwestern Canada, occasionally elsewhere', 'Splugorth; Naruni; Vampires; demon lords', 'mortals; Native American warriors and Shamans in general; the Nunnehi (spirits) in particular; gargoyles and dragons (viewed as rivals)', NULL, 'Cruel, bird-like humanoids who kidnap mortal women and hire out as mercenary enforcers for demons and evil gods from a hidden cloud realm.', 'Rifts World Book 15: Spirit West p.108-110');
INSERT INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'animal-man-monster', 'Animal Man-Monster', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Evil only; typically diabolic or miscreant', '{"IQ":"3D6","ME":"3D6","MA":"3D6","PS":"3D6+2D6","PP":"3D6+1D4","PE":"3D6+1D6","PB":"3D6","Spd":"3D6+3D6"}', NULL, NULL, NULL, '1D4x10+30', 'ME+6D6', 'Attributes shown are modifiers ADDED to the human''s original attributes, not standalone totals: M.E. is reduced 10%, M.A. reduced 25%, P.B. reduced 50% (except in human guise); I.Q. is unchanged. M.D.C. equals the former human''s hit points + S.D.C. points, plus Totem Power bonuses (giant animal form adds another +100 M.D.C.); +10 P.P.E. per level of experience.', NULL, 16, '{"attacks":6,"initiative":5,"strike":1,"pull":2}', 'Six physical or psionic attacks per melee round, or two by magic. +4 save vs poison; immune to disease, possession, and horror factor; bonuses are cumulative with Totem Animal bonuses. Vulnerable: weapons/attacks affecting the senses (sonic, chemical sprays, powerful odors) have doubled duration/penalty/damage; Demon Slaying weapons and those made from the Millennium Tree do double damage.', 'Retains only the Hand to Hand Combat skill (bonuses and combat moves, not extra attacks) and half of its other former O.C.C. skills (not related/secondary skills), frozen at whatever proficiency they were at transformation.', 'All powers of its Totem Animal; leaps an extra 10 ft; nightvision 2,000 ft; climbs 80/75%, swims 60%; resists heat; bio-regenerates 6D6 M.D.C./minute; can assume human guise or a giant totem-animal form with bonus M.D.C., speed, damage, and an attack.', 'Summon and control animal (of its Totem Species only), repel animals, and domination; all cost P.P.E.', 'Sense evil, sense magic, sixth sense, mind block, alter aura, death trance', '7-8 ft (2.1-2.4 m); some totem species (bears) can be twice that', '275-400 lbs of muscle', 'A supernatural abomination with a life of at least 1,000 years, though fewer than 25% live more than 100-200 years before being hunted down', 'Anywhere, from wilderness and small villages to the ''Burbs of Chi-Town and mega-city alleys; lairs are usually in the wilderness, caves, ruins, or subterranean dwellings', 'weaker evil beings used as minions/stooges; powerful evil beings it serves (or vice versa); demons and evil dragons especially', 'innocent, good, heroic beings; Totem Warriors; good Shamans; good spirits and gods', NULL, 'A human corrupted by stolen totem-spirit power into a hulking half-animal predator, paranoid, hyper-alert, and driven to kill.', 'Rifts World Book 15: Spirit West p.112-113');
INSERT INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'plant-man-monster', 'Plant Man-Monster', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Evil only; typically diabolic or miscreant', '{"IQ":"3D6","ME":"3D6","MA":"3D6+1D4","PS":"3D6+2D6","PP":"3D6","PE":"3D6+2D4","PB":"3D6","Spd":"3D6"}', NULL, NULL, NULL, '1D4x10+30', NULL, 'Attributes shown are modifiers ADDED to the human''s original attributes: M.E. is reduced 20%, Spd reduced 20%; I.Q. and P.P. unchanged. M.D.C. equals the former human''s hit points + S.D.C., plus Totem Powers; giant tree form adds +100 M.D.C. +25 per level of experience (maintainable 15 minutes/level); +10 P.P.E. per level of experience. Racial limitation: only humans, True Atlanteans, Elves, Ogres, or Psi-Stalkers can become one.', NULL, 15, '{"attacks":4,"parry":3,"pull":3}', 'Four physical attacks per melee round, or two by magic. +3 save vs poison; immune to disease, possession, and horror factor. Vulnerable: double damage from fire and magical cold; needs 8+ hours of sunlight and at least a glass of water a day (a gallon is better) or weakens (loses combat bonuses, speed, damage, attacks, and 40 M.D.C./week) until it hibernates or dies; cannot swim, sinks like a rock. Demon Slaying weapons and those made from the Millennium Tree do double damage.', 'Retains only the Hand to Hand Combat skill (bonuses and combat moves, not extra attacks) and half of its other former O.C.C. skills (not related/secondary skills), frozen at whatever proficiency they were at transformation.', 'Sees infrared/ultraviolet light to 4,000 ft, but poor night vision; climbs 95/90%; resists heat/cold; regenerates 1D4x10 M.D.C./minute, severed limbs in days, or head/body in weeks; can assume human guise or a giant tree form with extra limbs.', 'Repel animals, plant growth, nourish plants, plant spirit blessing, and plant travel; all cost P.P.E.', NULL, '8-10 ft (2.4-3 m); half human, half plant', '400-600 lbs (180-270 kg); x10 when giant-sized', 'A supernatural abomination with a life of at least 2,000 years, possibly immortal, though only half live more than 500 years before being hunted down', 'Anywhere, from wilderness and small villages to the ''Burbs of Chi-Town and mega-city alleys, but generally prefers or lives near forests', 'weaker evil beings used as minions/stooges; powerful evil beings it serves (or vice versa); demons and evil dragons especially', 'innocent, good, heroic beings; Totem Warriors; good Shamans; good spirits and gods', NULL, 'A human transformed by stolen plant-spirit power into a half-plant giant, cold and dispassionate, whose schemes take a long time to unfold.', 'Rifts World Book 15: Spirit West p.114-115');
INSERT INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'spirit-man-monster', 'Spirit Man-Monster', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Evil only; typically diabolic or miscreant', '{"IQ":"3D6+1D6","ME":"3D6","MA":"3D6","PS":"3D6+1D6","PP":"3D6","PE":"3D6","PB":"3D6","Spd":"3D6"}', NULL, NULL, '1D6x10', '2D4x100', '1D4x10+ME', 'Attributes shown are modifiers ADDED to the human''s original attributes: Spd is reduced 10%; other attributes unchanged. M.D.C. is the former human''s hit points + S.D.C. plus 1D6x10, and +10 per level of experience. +30 P.P.E. per level of experience. +2D4 I.S.P. per level of experience. Rarest of the three Man-Monsters, about 1 for every 50 of the others.', NULL, 14, '{"attacks":4}', 'Four physical or psionic attacks per melee round, or three by magic. +1D6 to supernatural P.S. when in energy form. Totem bonuses: +2 save vs magic, +5 save vs magical illusions, impervious to possession, all Ley Line Walker abilities at 3x range and +10% proficiency. In Energy Being form: +2 additional attacks per melee, +3 initiative, hovers/flies 300 mph, energy attacks do half damage, only harmed by magic/energy weapons. Vulnerable: double damage from magic weapons, triple from Millennium Tree weapons; negate magic does 2D4x10 M.D.; anti-magic cloud or a Ley Line Storm halves its M.D.C., attacks, bonuses, and spell strength.', 'Retains only the Hand to Hand Combat skill (bonuses and combat moves, not extra attacks) and half of its other former O.C.C. skills (not related/secondary skills), frozen at whatever proficiency they were at transformation.', 'Natural spellcaster; sees magic energy, energy beings, astral beings, and the invisible; regenerates 1D4x10 M.D.C./minute; impervious to poison, heat, cold, fatigue, disease, horror factor; can go astral, enter dreams, or become pure energy.', 'All energy-based wizard/common spells (per Rifts RPG p.167): blinding flash, globe of daylight, energy bolt, fuel flame, ignite fire, energy field, fire bolt, circle of flame, energy disruption, call lightning, fireball, impervious to energy, dispel magic barrier, life drain, negate magic, and anti-magic cloud; plus 1D6 additional spells per level from almost any magic category except Techno-Wizardry and Bio-Wizardry/Rune Magic.', 'All psionic sensitive abilities, plus telekinesis: super, psi-shield, and psi-sword', 'Average human size', '120-180 lbs (54-81 kg)', 'Immortal; cannot die of natural causes, but can be slain by violence or magic', 'Anywhere, from wilderness to big cities, wherever it can find people to worship it as a self-styled god', 'evil sorcerers; dragons; supernatural beings subservient to it', 'innocent, good, heroic beings; those of Native American heritage; above all, anyone who defies or challenges it', NULL, 'The rarest Man-Monster: a shaman who devoured stolen ancestor-spirit energy, becoming an immortal, godlike husk animated by magic.', 'Rifts World Book 15: Spirit West p.116-118');
INSERT INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'hunter-great-little-ones', 'Hunter Great Little Ones', 'faerie', 'rifts', 0, 'Principled or Scrupulous only', '{"IQ":"3D6","ME":"3D6+6","MA":"3D6+3","PS":"2D6+8","PP":"3D6+4","PE":"3D6+4","PB":"2D6+8","Spd":"4D6+58"}', NULL, NULL, '1D6x10+PE', 'PEx6', '2D6x10+ME', 'All physical attributes are supernatural. If a 19-20 is rolled for P.S., add another 1D6. +2D4 M.D.C. per level of experience. +20 P.P.E. per level of experience. +1D6 I.S.P. per level of experience. Spd is typically about 50 mph/80 kph.', NULL, 10, '{"attacks":5,"initiative":5,"strike":3,"parry":1,"dodge":3,"disarm":3,"roll":6}', 'Five physical or five psionic attacks per round (can combine types up to five total), or two attacks by magic. +3 to parry using any ancient weapon; +1 save vs psionic attack; +4 save vs horror factor; +2 save vs poison and magic. Vulnerable to any net (completely restrains it and blocks escape artist) and to poison, toxins, drugs, and alcohol. Destroyed only if M.D.C. is reduced 60+ points below zero or it is decapitated, otherwise it regenerates.', 'Effectively a hunter and wilderness scout. All wilderness skills at 90%, plus basic math, fishing, ritual dance/sing, streetwise, camouflage, detect ambush/concealment, escape artist, intelligence, track humanoids, wilderness survival, prowl, swim, climb, gymnastics, horsemanship: exotic (small animals, -20% on birds), all at 74%+2%/level; archery, paired weapons, all ancient weapons, tiny flintlock guns and tiny Cavalry Repeating rifles; magically speaks/understands all languages at 94%.', 'Outruns all game animals; heals 1D6 points every two hours; nightvision 400 ft; breathes without air; impervious to fatigue, heat, cold, disease, and possession.', 'Astral projection (can carry one extra person per 20 P.P.E. spent), sense evil, sense magic, death trance, chameleon, climb, commune with spirits, concealment, eyes of the wolf, invisibility: superior, multiple image, speed of the snail, summon and control canines, repel animals, and energy disruption; also makes and activates all minor fetishes and the major fetishes of great song, great speed, great tracking, wing-flight, and great tooth & claw.', 'All sensitive abilities, plus psychic diagnosis, psychic surgery, deaden pain, group mind block, and mind block auto-defense', '12 inches (0.3 m)', '2 lbs (0.9 kg)', 'Immortal, but can be destroyed through violence', 'Anywhere in North America, particularly wilderness areas and regions inhabited by Native Americans', 'other spirits, lesser and greater; fellow Great Little Ones; some Native American Gods; Native Americans in general, particularly Pure Ones and devoted Traditionalists', 'the forces of evil; dark spirits; evil Shamans; supernatural monsters; rivals and enemies of Native Americans', NULL, 'A tiny, ancient ancestor-spirit who watches over hunters and animals, quietly aiding worthy heroes and punishing cruelty to wildlife.', 'Rifts World Book 15: Spirit West p.138-140');
INSERT INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'stone-thrower-great-little-ones', 'Stone Thrower Great Little Ones', 'faerie', 'rifts', 0, 'Most are scrupulous, a few principled or unprincipled', '{"IQ":"3D6","ME":"3D6+2","MA":"3D6+2","PS":"2D6+20","PP":"2D6+7","PE":"2D6+8","PB":"3D6","Spd":"3D6+6"}', NULL, NULL, '2D6x10+PE', 'PEx5', '3D4x10+ME', 'All physical attributes are supernatural. If a 28-32 is rolled for P.S., add another 1D6. +2D6 M.D.C. per level of experience. +20 P.P.E. per level of experience. +2D6 I.S.P. per level of experience.', NULL, 10, '{"attacks":6,"initiative":4,"strike":4,"parry":2,"disarm":4,"roll":4,"pull":4}', 'Six physical or six psionic attacks per round (can combine types up to six total), or two attacks by magic. +4 to parry using any ancient weapon; +1 save vs psionic attack; +5 save vs horror factor; +2 save vs poison and magic. Loses its supernatural strength, attributes, and spell casting if removed from contact with the earth (suspended, thrown, lifted by someone with greater P.S.); also vulnerable to drugs, magic potions, and alcohol. Destroyed only if M.D.C. is reduced 80+ points below zero or it is decapitated, otherwise it regenerates.', 'Effectively a Warrior. All wilderness skills at 80%, plus anthropology, archeology, ritual dance/sing, detect ambush/concealment, intelligence, track humanoids, wilderness survival, swim, climb, prowl, boxing, wrestling, horsemanship: exotic (-25% on birds), prospecting, recognize weapon quality, military fortification, trap construction, trap/mine detection, whittling/sculpting, and basic math, all at 74-80%+2%/level; archery, paired weapons, all ancient weapons, tiny flintlock gun and tiny Cavalry Repeating rifle; magically speaks/understands all languages at 94%.', 'Needs no leverage to lift, throw, or carry objects of any size at full strength; nightvision 400 ft; impervious to fatigue, heat, cold, disease, possession, magical petrification; can ride any small wild animal as if tame.', 'Astral projection (can carry one extra person per 20 P.P.E. spent), commune with spirits, fool''s gold, climb, ignite flame, concealment, chameleon, invisibility: simple, dispel magic barrier, impervious to energy, invulnerability, sense evil, sense magic, stone to flesh, teleport: lesser, and familiar link; also makes and activates all minor fetishes and the major fetishes of great armor, great body, supernatural damage, supernatural strength, and great tooth & claw.', 'All physical-category psionics, plus bio-regenerate, object read, sixth sense, mind bolt, psi-shield, and telekinesis (super)', '13-15 inches (0.35-0.38 m)', '4 lbs (1.8 kg)', 'Immortal, but can be destroyed through violence', 'Anywhere in North America, particularly wilderness areas and regions inhabited by Native Americans', 'other spirits, lesser and greater; fellow Great Little Ones; some Native American Gods; Native Americans in general, particularly Pure Ones and devoted Traditionalists', 'the forces of evil; dark spirits; evil Shamans; supernatural monsters; rivals and enemies of Native Americans', NULL, 'A stocky ancestor-spirit guardian, quiet and reserved, who hurls stones and boulders to defend Native peoples, animals, and the Deep Earth.', 'Rifts World Book 15: Spirit West p.140-141');
INSERT INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'nurturer-great-little-ones', 'Nurturer Great Little Ones', 'faerie', 'rifts', 0, 'Most are principled, a few scrupulous or unprincipled', '{"IQ":"3D6","ME":"3D6+4","MA":"3D6+6","PS":"2D6+6","PP":"2D6+7","PE":"2D6+8","PB":"3D6+6","Spd":"3D6+12"}', NULL, NULL, '1D4x10+PE', 'PEx6', '3D4x10+ME', 'All physical attributes are supernatural. If a 16-18 is rolled for P.S., add another 1D6. +2D6 M.D.C. per level of experience. +25 P.P.E. per level of experience. +12 I.S.P. per level of experience.', NULL, 10, '{"attacks":4,"initiative":2,"strike":1,"parry":1,"disarm":2,"roll":4,"pull":4}', 'Four physical or four psionic attacks per round (can combine types up to four total), or two attacks by magic. +3 to parry using a staff; +1 save vs psionic attack; +2 save vs horror factor; +1 save vs magic. Vulnerable to lack of sunlight: no shamanic plant magic after 24 hours of darkness, no magic and half-strength psionics after a week, half melee attacks/speed/bonuses, and starting on the 15th day of darkness it dies at 2D4 M.D.C./day unless returned to the sun (which heals 3D6 immediately). Has the alcohol tolerance of a Saloon Bum. Destroyed only if M.D.C. is reduced 40+ points below zero or it is decapitated, otherwise it regenerates.', 'Effectively a Healer/Doctor and caretaker. Botany, basic math, identify plants & fruit, preserve food, cook, holistic medicine, pathology, brewing, cattle/animal lore, breed dogs, and animal husbandry at 90%+1%/level; plus fishing, art, dance, sing, play wind instrument, skin/prepare animal hides, intelligence, land navigation, wilderness survival, all lores, swim, climb, prowl, acrobatics, and horsemanship: exotic (prefers birds, -5% in the air) at 74-76%+2%/level; magically speaks/understands all languages at 94%.', 'Nightvision 400 ft; impervious to fatigue, heat, cold, disease, poison, drugs, possession; an innate sense locates edible plants for miles; can ride any small wild animal, including birds, as if it were tame.', 'Astral projection (can carry one extra person per 20 P.P.E. spent), commune with spirits, sense evil, sense magic, charismatic aura, ignite flame, fuel flame, extinguish fire, chameleon, impervious to energy, breathe without air, call lightning, heal wounds, cure illness, purification (food and water), water to wine, and all Plant Shaman magic spells; also makes and activates the minor fetishes of healing, heritage and self, luck, porcupine quill, song, swim, sure-footedness, and wing, plus the major fetishes of great healing, great luck, great song, medicine bundle, and shapechange.', 'All psionic abilities from the healing category, plus see aura, empathy, empathic transmission, hydrokinesis, bio-regeneration (super), group mind block, psi-shield, and mind block auto-defense', '12 inches (0.3 m)', '1-2 lbs (0.45-0.9 kg)', 'Immortal, but can be destroyed through violence', 'Anywhere in North America, particularly wilderness areas and regions inhabited by Native Americans', 'other spirits, lesser and greater; fellow Great Little Ones; some Native American Gods; Native Americans in general, particularly Pure Ones and devoted Traditionalists', 'the forces of evil; dark spirits; evil Shamans; supernatural monsters; rivals and enemies of Native Americans', NULL, 'A gentle plant-tending ancestor-spirit and healer who befriends the kind, feeds the hungry, and fiercely defends children and the innocent.', 'Rifts World Book 15: Spirit West p.141-142');
INSERT INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'plumed-serpents', 'Plumed Serpents', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Any; tends unprincipled, anarchist, miscreant', '{"IQ":"3D6+4","ME":"3D6+6","MA":"3D6","PS":"3D6+12","PP":"3D6+6","PE":"3D6+8","PB":"2D6+2","Spd":"3D6"}', NULL, NULL, '1D4x100+200', 'PEx10', '3D4x10+ME', 'Spd is 3D6 on the ground or 1D4x10+40 flying. M.D.C. by location (adult): Head 120, Clawed feet (2) 100 each, Wings (2) 160 each, Main Body 1D4x100+200 (used as mdc above). P.P.E. gets +10/level if a spell caster. I.S.P. gets +2D4/level. Young/PC variant: size 30 ft, M.D.C. 100+PE attribute+2D6/level, starts 1st-2nd level, Horror Factor 11. Young also: bite 3D6 M.D., breath 3D6+2 M.D. at half range, bio-regen 3D6/min.', NULL, 14, '{"attacks":6,"initiative":1,"strike":1,"dodge":3,"roll":2}', '+2 to save vs poison and disease, +1 to save vs magic (+3 if spell caster), +3 to save vs horror factor (+3 more as adult); -30% chance for others to surprise it via prowl, half penalty when blinded; -25% on skills needing human hands/dexterity unless in human form. Vulnerable: double damage from weapons made of dragon/demon bone or Millennium Tree wood; tends irritable, arrogant, short-tempered.; attacks per melee: Six physical and/or psionic attacks per melee round, or two by magic; dodge: +3 when flying; roll: +2 (impact, punch, or fall)', 'R.C.C.: detect concealment, intelligence, wilderness survival, prowl, swimming, track (humanoids), land navigation, two languages, all at +10%; natural language Dragonese 94%. Plus six Secondary Skills from Domestic, Military, Physical (not H2H/boxing), Rogue, Technical, W.P. (human form only), Wilderness; about 15% study magic instead.', 'Nightvision 1200 ft, heightened hearing/smell, exceptional sight, flight, bio-regenerates 6D6 M.D.C./min (3D6 young), hard to surprise, half penalty when blinded, metamorphosis into human form (limited changes/day), invisibility 3x/day, burrows into loose soil or sand.', 'None to start; about 15% instead learn ley line/wizard magic (Ley Line Walker abilities #5-6; four spells at level one, two more at levels 2-4, one more per level after).', 'Major psionic: six psychic abilities from any category except super (one may be from super); one additional super or two lesser abilities at levels 3, 6, 9, 12, 15+.', '60-70 ft (18-21 m) long; young are half that', '1-2 tons', '750-1000 years; matures around age 300', 'Deserts and hot, arid regions; can be found anywhere', 'Other Plumed Serpents (overlapping/shared territory); Human and D-bee worshippers', 'None natural; accumulates foes through territorial disputes', 'O.C.C. not applicable; may instead opt for limited spell-casting ability in place of the skill selections', 'A giant feathered desert-dwelling serpent-dragon that rules vast territories, fighting with lightning breath, tactics, and magic.', 'Rifts World Book 15: Spirit West p.118-120');
INSERT INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'stone-giants', 'Stone Giants', 'giant', 'rifts', 0, 'Evil only; typically diabolic or miscreant', '{"IQ":"3D6","ME":"2D6","MA":"1D6","PS":"20+3D6","PP":"3D6","PE":"3D6+6","PB":"2D4","Spd":"3D6+6"}', NULL, NULL, 'PEx6', '120', 'MEx2', 'M.D.C. gets +2D6 per level of experience (base P.E.x6). P.P.E. gets +2D6 per each level of experience (base 120). Wisps of Sickness: 2-5 wisps cause a magical-sickness-like effect at double duration, at no P.P.E. cost, usable once per melee round. Death Ghost Attack: spirit-based attack that bypasses armor/vehicles/force fields, costs 80 P.P.E., attacks for 1D4+1 rounds per level, hits up to 2 targets within 60 ft, drains the victim''s P.P.E. to zero causing a fatal spirit disease (cures: Medicine Lodge ritual 500 P.P.E., Restoration ritual 750 P.P.E., or resurrection by a great spirit/god).', NULL, 15, '{"attacks":5,"initiative":1,"parry":1,"roll":2}', '+4 to save vs horror factor, +4 to save vs poison (in addition to attribute bonuses). Vulnerable: cannot swim, sinks like a rock.; attacks per melee: Five physical or psionic attacks per melee round; roll: +2 (impact, punch, or fall); damage: As per supernatural P.S.', 'R.C.C. & Skills: W.P. Blunt, W.P. Spear, horsemanship: Exotic animals, camouflage, all Wilderness skills at +10%; speaks Gobblely 90%. Plus six skills from Domestic, Espionage, Rogue, W.P., and lore/language skills from Technical.', 'Keen vision, nightvision 400 ft, climb 90/80%, resists normal heat/fire/cold (half damage; full from magic/M.D. fire), immune to disease, regenerates 2D6 M.D.C./hour, regrows lost limbs in 1D4 months.', NULL, 'All psionic healing abilities', '10-12 ft (3-3.6 m)', '800-1200 lbs (360-540 kg)', '150-200 years', 'Northern or mountainous forest wilderness; rare south of Wyoming/Dakotas except along the Rockies', 'None per se; occasionally ally with other supernatural or powerful beings', 'No natural enemies; hated and feared by races they prey on (humans, Psi-Stalkers, Simvan)', NULL, 'A huge, rock-crusted forest-dwelling predator that inflicts a lingering, near-incurable spirit sickness that drains P.P.E. and prevents healing.', 'Rifts World Book 15: Spirit West p.120-121');
INSERT INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'teepowka', 'Teepowka', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Considered miscreant; a supernatural predator', '{"IQ":"1D4+3","ME":"2D6+8","MA":"1D6","PS":"25+5D6","PP":"3D6","PE":"20+2D6","PB":"1D4+1","Spd":"1D6x10+40"}', NULL, NULL, '300+PEx10', 'PEx2', NULL, 'I.Q. is low compared to humans but it is a cunning predator using lion-like stalking/ambush tactics; usually a lone hunter, sometimes a mated pair (1D4 young every 10 years) or a loose-knit pride of 3D4.', NULL, 14, '{"attacks":4,"initiative":2,"strike":2,"parry":1,"roll":3}', '+6 to save vs horror factor, +10 to save vs poison and disease (in addition to any attribute bonuses).; attacks per melee: Four attacks per melee round; parry: +1 (with horns); roll: +3 (punch/fall); damage: As per supernatural P.S. from kicks, stomps, and butts with head or horns', NULL, 'M.D.C. armor and limited chameleon-like camouflage (70% visual prowl), land navigation 90%, track animals 60%, track humanoids 70%, track by smell 60%, nightvision 200 ft, swim 40%.', NULL, NULL, '18-20 ft (5.4-6 m) tall, 20-25 ft (5.4-7.5 m) long', '8-12 tons', '40-60 years', 'Virtually any terrain west of the Mississippi and south of Calgary; mainly Western Wilderness, Mexico, parts of South America', 'None per se; occasionally ally with other intelligent predators or powerful beings', 'Predatory dinosaurs and humans (also considered prey)', NULL, 'A six-legged, heavily armored plains carnivore that rams and tramples prey and is immune to Simvan mind control.', 'Rifts World Book 15: Spirit West p.122-123');
INSERT INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'two-faced-star-people', 'Two-Faced Star-People', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'All evil, typically miscreant and diabolic; rare aberrant instances', '{"IQ":"3D6+1","ME":"3D6+6","MA":"3D6","PS":"3D6","PP":"3D6","PE":"3D6+4","PB":"1D6","Spd":"3D6+6"}', NULL, '3D4x10', NULL, '1D4x10+30+PE', '3D4x10+ME', 'Attributes given are for natural form; while duplicating someone it has eaten, it takes on that victim''s physical attributes. Hit Points: standard for natural form; add the creature''s P.E. to the hit points of any copied form. S.D.C. adds 2D4x10 to the S.D.C. of copied forms. P.P.E. gets +2D6 per level of experience. Average Experience Level: 1D4+2. It is an S.D.C. creature and must rely on M.D. weapons, armor, or magic items to defend itself; combat expertise varies with the victim currently duplicated.', NULL, 14, '{"attacks":5,"strike":1,"parry":1,"roll":2}', '+4 to save vs psionics, +2 to save vs magic, +3 to save vs horror factor, +1 to save vs poison and disease (in addition to attribute bonuses).; Horror Factor applies only once its true nature is known; attacks per melee: Five physical or psionic attacks per melee in natural form, plus any additional attacks/skills/bonuses from a duplicated victim; roll: +2 (impact)', 'O.C.C. effectively Vagabond; when exact duplication is used, gains all skills of the victim, frozen at the level held at the moment of death.', 'Instant shapechanging into any 5-7 ft humanoid at no P.P.E. cost, indefinite until badly hurt or knocked out; Exact Duplication by Consumption (40 P.P.E.): devouring a humanoid perfectly copies its body, scent, DNA, and most memories (except the last 48 hours) and natural/super abilities.', NULL, 'Major psionic: detect psionics, hypnotic suggestion, mind block, see aura, sixth sense, alter aura, total recall; super abilities mentally possess others and mind wipe. All function at 7th level proficiency regardless of the creature''s actual experience.', '6-6.5 ft (1.8-2 m) in natural form; varies with copied forms', '150-200 lb (67.5-90 kg)', 'Potentially immortal via body-swapping; ages normally per the race currently copied', 'Can be encountered anywhere; prefers crowded cities and communities', 'None per se; occasionally ally with other supernatural beings or powerful sorcerers (work as assassins/spies)', 'Cheyenne; Cyber-Knights; Cosmo-Knights; hated and feared by most races', 'Effectively the Vagabond O.C.C.; gains a duplicated victim''s frozen skill set while wearing that form', 'A shapeshifting, other-dimensional man-eater that perfectly duplicates any human or D-bee it devours to infiltrate unnoticed.', 'Rifts World Book 15: Spirit West p.123-124');
INSERT INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'ukt-water-serpents', 'Ukt Water Serpents', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Any, but good is almost unheard of; usually evil, occasionally anarchist', '{"IQ":"3D6","ME":"3D6+3","MA":"3D6","PS":"4D6+12","PP":"3D6+2","PE":"3D6+8","PB":"1D4+2","Spd":"3D6+10"}', NULL, NULL, '240+PEx10', '3D6x10', '2D4x10+ME', 'Spd 3D6+10 is on dry land; swimming Spd is 135, about 90 mph (140 km). M.D.C. gets +1D4x10 per level of experience. P.P.E. gets +20 per level of experience. I.S.P. gets +10 points per level of experience.', NULL, 15, '{"attacks":6,"initiative":3,"strike":3,"parry":3,"dodge":2,"roll":2,"pull":2}', '+2 to save vs magic, +6 to save vs poison and drugs, +4 to save vs horror factor (in addition to attribute and other bonuses).; attacks per melee: Six physical or psionic attacks per melee, two by magic; roll: +2 (impact); pull: +2 (pull punch); damage: As per supernatural P.S.', 'R.C.C. & Skills: W.P. sword, W.P. blunt, prowl, wilderness survival, all Wilderness skills at +10%; basic math 95%; speaks Dragonese, Gobblely, and American at 90%. Plus eight skills from Domestic, Espionage, Military, Rogue, Technical, W.P.', 'Survives depths of 3 miles, dives to 1000 ft, breathes water and air, nightvision/infrared/thermal 1000 ft, sonar-like echolocation, tracks by smell 60%, immune to cold and disease, bio-regenerates 3D6 M.D.C./round, regrows tail/fins/limbs in 3D4 days, coiling/constricting body, prehensile tail.', 'Possesses all water elemental spells, levels 1-5', 'Choose ten abilities from any of the three lesser categories, plus three super-psionic abilities', 'Stands about 12 ft (3.6 m); overall body length 60-100 ft (18.3-30.5 m)', '1-2 tons', '300-500 years', 'Large freshwater lakes and rivers (Great Lakes, Lake Nipagon, Lake Manitoba, Great Slave Lake, Great Bear Lake); also salty oceans/gulfs including Gulf of Mexico', 'The God Uktena and the Splugorth (serve as minions); True dragons, powerful supernatural beings, powerful sorcerers', 'Humans in general; The Coalition Army specifically; Thunderbird and his children; Enemies of their master', NULL, 'A huge, armor-plated serpentine water monster allied to the god Uktena, feared for its lethal venom and crushing coils.', 'Rifts World Book 15: Spirit West p.125-126');
INSERT INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'wendigo', 'Wendigo', 'monster', 'rifts', 1, 'Any, but most are good; gentle, compassionate, caring', '{"IQ":"3D6","ME":"3D6+2","MA":"3D6+4","PS":"3D6+10","PP":"3D6","PE":"3D6+4","PB":"2D6+4","Spd":"3D6+6"}', NULL, NULL, 'PEx5', 'PEx3', NULL, 'M.D.C. gets +1D6 per level of experience (Wendigo were hit point/S.D.C. creatures before the Coming of the Rifts). P.P.E. gets +2D6 per level of experience. Average Level of Experience (NPC): 1D4+3.', NULL, 10, '{"initiative":2,"dodge":1,"roll":2,"pull":3}', '+2 to save vs poison and disease, +1 to save vs magic, +2 to save vs possession, +3 to save vs horror factor (in addition to attribute and O.C.C. bonuses).; attacks per melee: As per O.C.C., plus +1 attack/action per melee round; roll: +2 (impact); pull: +3 (pull punch); damage: As per supernatural P.S.', 'R.C.C. Skills (regardless of O.C.C.): Swim, climb, camouflage, wilderness survival, detect ambush all at +20%, prowl at +10%.', 'Nightvision/infrared/thermal vision 1000 ft, keen eyesight/hearing/smell, tracks by smell 40%+5%/level, recognizes scent 30%+4%/level, half damage from cold, heals at double the human rate, Minor Dimensional Doorway teleport (once/day/level, range 100+20 ft/level, costs 10 P.P.E.).', 'Natural powers: death trance, chameleon, shadow meld, escape, concealment, detect concealment, dowsing, repel animals, purification of food and water.', 'Standard, same as humans (see page 12 of the Rifts RPG)', '7-8 ft (2.1-2.4 m) tall', '250-400 lbs (112.5-180 kg)', '650 years', 'Deep, remote forests and mountain slopes across North America (US, Canada, and unknown to most, northern Russia)', 'Nunnehi and other spirits; Spirit and Totem Warriors (travel together on quests)', 'Evil supernatural beings; Trespassers/despoilers proven genuinely dangerous to the Wendigo, their sites, friends, or innocents', 'Available O.C.C.s: Plant, Animal, or Elemental Shaman, or Tribal or Totem Warrior (as Indians); or Wilderness Scout, Vagabond, Bandit, or Farmer at half the usual Related O.C.C. skills; leans away from high-tech skills and never uses artificial augmentation.', 'A large, gentle, fur-covered forest humanoid known as Sasquatch or Big Foot, a loyal ally of Native American spirits who guards sacred sites.', 'Rifts World Book 15: Spirit West p.126-128');
INSERT INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'lesser-animal-spirits', 'Lesser Animal Spirits', 'spirit', 'rifts', 0, 'Good/unprincipled typical (10% anarchist, 5% aberrant, 2% other evil)', '{"IQ":"2D6+4","ME":"2D6+4","MA":"2D6+4"}', '3D6', '2D6', NULL, '2D4x10', 'MEx3', 'Physical attributes (PS/PP/PE/PB/Spd) are roughly the totem animal''s, supernatural when materialized, mortal/SDC when possessed. HP tiers by totem size: 1D6 tiny, 2D6 small, 3D6 medium/fox-size (used above), 6D6 large. SDC tiers: 1D4 tiny, 2D4 small, 2D6 medium (used above), 5D6 large. MDC (materialized or energy form) = combined HP+SDC of totem +18, not expressible as a single formula. PPE +20/level of experience. ISP +10/level. HF = totem animal''s HF +1.', NULL, NULL, '{"initiative":1,"pull":2}', '+1 save vs magic, +2 save vs horror factor (in addition to attribute/OCC bonuses).', 'Basic Math, land navigation, track animals, skin/preserve hides, preserve food, dance, sing, intelligence, prowl, climb, lore: cattle/animals, lore: Indians, lore: demons/monsters, all 80%+2%/level; speaks all languages 90%.', 'Possesses or materializes into its totem animal species; supernatural traits when materialized, mortal traits when possessing a body; regenerates in energy form; shares the standard traits common to all spirits.', 'Repel animal, dowsing, purification (food and water), familiar link, plus 1D4+1 spells per level from Shamanic or common magic, levels 1-5.', 'All Psionic Sensitive abilities plus one Physical ability per level of experience.', 'Varies with the totem animal species.', 'Varies with the totem animal species.', 'Immortal; can be destroyed only while in energy form.', 'Anywhere in North America, especially wilderness and Native American regions.', 'Other spirits (lesser and greater); some Native American Gods; Native Americans, especially Pure Ones and Traditionalists', 'Forces of evil; dark spirits; evil Shamans; supernatural monsters; rivals/enemies of Native Americans', NULL, 'A minor Native American nature spirit that can possess or take the form of a small animal to help and watch over indigenous peoples.', 'Rifts World Book 15: Spirit West p.132-134');
INSERT INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'lesser-plant-spirits', 'Lesser Plant Spirits', 'spirit', 'rifts', 0, 'Good/unprincipled typical (8% anarchist, 4% aberrant, 1% other evil)', '{"IQ":"2D6+3","ME":"2D6+6","MA":"2D6+2"}', '3D6', '1D6', NULL, '3D4x10', 'MEx3', 'Physical attributes are roughly the totem plant''s, supernatural when materialized, mortal/SDC when possessed; can move/scurry at Spd 2 (small plants/bushes) or 4 (trees) when materialized. HP tiers: 1D4 tiny flower/mushroom, 2D4 small plant, 3D6 bush/shrub/vine (used above), 2D4x10 large bush, 5D6x10 average tree, 3D6x100 old/tall tree. SDC tiers: 1 tiny, 1D4 small, 1D6 bush/vine (used above), 4D6 large bush, 3D6x10 tree. AR: 4 small plants, 7 bushes/vines (used above), 8 large bushes, 9 small trees, 10-12 large trees. MDC = combined HP+SDC +20/level of the spirit, not expressible as one formula. PPE +15/level. ISP +10/level. HF is typically none unless recognized as a spirit, then HF 10.', 7, NULL, NULL, '+1 save vs psionics, +2 save vs magic, +2 save vs horror factor (in addition to attribute/OCC bonuses); possessed plants are vulnerable to poison and physical attacks that kill the host.', 'Basic Math, astronomy, identify plants/fruits, carpentry, botany, preserve food, cook, camouflage, lore: cattle/animals, lore: Indians, lore: demons/monsters, all 80%+1%/level; holistic medicine 70%+1%/level; speaks all languages 90%.', 'Possesses or materializes into its totem plant; can move or use limbs/vines to grab or strike when materialized; regenerates in energy form; shares the standard traits common to all spirits.', 'Dowsing, spirit''s blessing (plant), nourish plants, animate forest floor, chameleon, plus 1D4 spells per level from Shamanic or common magic, levels 1-5.', 'Five Healing and five Psionic Sensitive abilities, plus one additional ability per level of experience.', 'Varies with the totem plant.', 'Varies with the totem plant.', 'Immortal; can be destroyed only while in energy form.', 'Anywhere in North America, especially wilderness and Native American regions.', 'Other spirits (lesser and greater); some Native American Gods; Native Americans, especially Pure Ones and Traditionalists', 'Forces of evil; dark spirits; evil Shamans; supernatural monsters; rivals/enemies of Native Americans', NULL, 'A quiet, secretive Native American plant-totem spirit that inhabits or takes the shape of a shrub, vine, or small plant.', 'Rifts World Book 15: Spirit West p.134-135');
INSERT INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'lesser-elemental-spirits', 'Lesser Elemental Spirits', 'spirit', 'rifts', 0, 'Good/unprincipled typical (5% anarchist, 3% aberrant, 1% other evil)', '{"IQ":"2D6+6","ME":"2D6+6","MA":"2D6+8","PS":"3D6+8","PP":"2D6+8","PE":"3D6+6","PB":"3D6+6","Spd":"3D6+6"}', 'PEx10', 'PEx3', NULL, 'PEx6', 'MEx4', 'Physical attributes apply only when materialized. HP is +40 more for a Fire totem and +100 more for an Earth totem. MDC (materialized or energy form) = combined HP+SDC, not expressible as one formula since pool names cannot be referenced. PPE +20/level of experience. ISP +12/level. Materialization lasts 90 min/level, +15 PPE/90 min to maintain. Appearance by element: Air=any bird, Fire=any predatory animal, Water=female Native American, Earth=male Native American.', NULL, 13, '{"attacks":4}', 'Physical-form bonuses vary by element (in addition to attribute bonuses): Air +1 attack/rd, +2 initiative, +3 dodge, +3 pull punch, +1 save magic, +1 save horror factor. Fire +2 attacks/rd, +3 initiative, +2 strike, +1 pull punch, +1 save magic, +5 save horror factor. Water +2 initiative, +1 parry/dodge, +4 pull punch, +1 save magic, +2 save horror factor. Earth +1 attack/rd, +1 initiative, +1 strike, +2 pull punch, +8 supernatural PS damage, +1 save magic, +3 save horror factor. Energy form: 2 spells or 4 psionic attacks or 4 actions per melee.', 'Skills differ by element (Air: astronomy/navigation/chemistry/etc; Fire: interrogation/dance/etc; Water: swim/boat building/etc; Earth: land navigation/holistic medicine/etc), all base skills 76-80% +1-2%/level; speaks all languages 88-92%.', 'Bio-regenerates 1D4x10 MDC/minute; understands True Elemental language; 01-80% chance to sense elemental/spirit forces within 500 ft; each element grants unique senses (weather, seismic activity, fire, or water) and matching resistances.', 'All Warlock spells of its element, levels 1-5; knows how to make/activate minor fetishes.', 'Telepathy plus, by element: Air=all Sensitive powers + electrokinesis; Fire=pyrokinesis, bio-manipulation, hypnotic suggestion, mind block; Water=all Healing powers + hydrokinesis; Earth=all Physical powers + psi-sword.', 'Same as the animal or human it imitates.', 'Roughly 20% more than the animal or human it imitates.', 'Immortal; can be destroyed only while in energy form.', 'Anywhere in North America, especially wilderness and Native American regions.', 'Other spirits (lesser and greater); some Native American Gods; Native Americans, especially Pure Ones and Traditionalists', 'Forces of evil; dark spirits; evil Shamans; supernatural monsters; rivals/enemies of Native Americans', NULL, 'A field-agent spirit of the Great Elementals, appearing as a bird, predatory animal, or young Native American depending on its air, fire, water, or earth nature.', 'Rifts World Book 15: Spirit West p.135-137');
INSERT INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'kachina-tectonic-spirit', 'Kachina Tectonic Spirit', 'spirit', 'rifts', 0, 'Principled/scrupulous typical (10% unprincipled, 2% anarchist, 2% aberrant evil)', '{"IQ":"2D6+4","ME":"2D6+6","MA":"1D6+4","PS":"1D6+8","PP":"1D6+8","PE":"1D6+8","Spd":"2D6+12"}', NULL, NULL, '2D6+6', '1D4x10', 'MEx2', 'Also known as the ''Doll Spirit.'' Physical attributes (PS/PP/PE/Spd) count only while it animates a Spirit Doll or some other object; PS is capped at a maximum of 16. SDC/MDC vary with the object animated: small toys ~2D6 SDC, medium (13-24 in) 3D6 SDC (+1D6 if especially tough, used above), large (25-36 in) 6D6 SDC (+2D6 if solid wood); inhabited-object MDC = combined HP+SDC of that object, not expressible as one formula - the ''2D6+6'' MDC given above is only the spirit''s own energy-form value. PPE +10/level of experience. ISP +6/level. Must have its doll body rebuilt (and be re-summoned) after losing 75% of its MDC or after 50 years of wear.; In S.D.C. settings: hit points 2D6+6, S.D.C. 3D6', NULL, NULL, '{"attacks":4,"initiative":2,"strike":1,"parry":1,"dodge":3,"pull":3,"roll":5}', '+2 save vs magic, +3 save vs earth and water elemental magic, +10 save vs horror factor. Horror Factor typically reflects the object animated, usually 9-11.', 'Basic Math, land navigation, dance, intelligence, surveillance (tail only), prowl, climb, lore: Indians, lore: demons/monsters, all 70%+2%/level; speaks all languages 90%.', 'Only form is a Kachina Spirit Doll (natural form: a small warm red energy sphere); hides its aura/essence from detection; regenerates 2D6 MDC/hour; communicates only by telepathy; must be summoned by a greater power, cannot materialize alone.', 'Four first-level Elemental Earth spells of choice, plus six other earth spells from levels 1-3.', 'Healing touch, mind block, presence sense, see aura, see the invisible, sense evil, telepathy (communication only), alter aura, summon inner strength.', 'Six inches to five feet (0.18 to 1.5 m); Spirit Dolls are typically 1-3 feet.', 'Varies with the item animated; Spirit Dolls typically 3-8 pounds.', 'Immortal; can be destroyed only while in energy form.', 'Anywhere, particularly among Native Americans.', 'Other Kachina spirits (lesser and greater); Kachina Dancers; Standing-Mountain and Hard-Woman-Dancing', 'Forces of evil; dark spirits; evil Shamans; supernatural monsters; enemies of those who summon it', NULL, 'The lowliest true Kachina spirit, called the Doll Spirit, summoned by a Kachina Dancer to secretly animate and guard a small wooden doll.', 'Rifts World Book 15: Spirit West p.145-146');
INSERT INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'lesser-kachina-spirit', 'Lesser Kachina Spirit', 'spirit', 'rifts', 0, 'Principled/scrupulous typical (4% unprincipled, 2% anarchist, 2% aberrant evil)', '{"IQ":"2D6+6","ME":"2D6+6","MA":"2D6+8","PS":"3D6+10","PP":"2D6+6","PE":"3D6+4","PB":"2D6+6","Spd":"3D6+6"}', 'PEx6+50', 'PEx10', NULL, 'PEx5', 'MEx3', 'Physical attributes apply only in a materialized body. MDC (materialized or energy form) = combined HP+SDC, not expressible as one formula since pool names cannot be referenced. PPE +15/level of experience. ISP +10/level. When it materializes it takes the shape of a Kachina Doll or of a burrower (mole, groundhog, prairie dog, rabbit, badger); can only possess burrowing animals.', NULL, 12, '{"attacks":4,"initiative":1,"strike":1,"pull":4,"roll":4}', '+1 save vs magic, +3 save vs earth and water elemental magic, +5 save vs horror factor.', 'All wilderness skills plus basic mathematics, wilderness survival, climb, swim, prowl, lore: magic/geomancy/ley lines, lore: Indians, lore: demons/monsters, all 70%+2%/level; speaks all languages 90%.', 'Bio-regenerates 4D6 MDC/minute; nightvision 600 ft; impervious to fatigue, poison, drugs, disease, heat, cold; conceals its aura/essence from detection; senses other Kachina spirits even when concealed inside a doll or animal.', 'All Earth Warlock spells, levels 1-3; cannot make or activate fetishes, but may deliver one on behalf of a greater spirit, god, or Kachina Dancer.', 'Six Physical category abilities plus mind block.', 'Same as the normal animal it is imitating.', 'Roughly 20% more than the animal imitated; typically 3-8 pounds as a doll.', 'Immortal; can be destroyed only while in energy form.', 'Anywhere in North America, especially wilderness and Native American regions.', 'Other Kachina spirits (lesser and greater); Kachina Dancers; Standing-Mountain and Hard-Woman-Dancing', 'Forces of evil; dark spirits; evil Shamans; supernatural monsters; enemies of those who summon it', NULL, 'A five-foot, glowing doll-like earth spirit of the Kachina family that can possess or become a burrowing animal.', 'Rifts World Book 15: Spirit West p.146-147');
INSERT INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'great-kachina-spirits', 'Great Kachina Spirits', 'spirit', 'rifts', 0, 'Any, mostly good; some evil/self-serving (e.g. Dark-Hand, aberrant evil)', '{"IQ":"3D6+8","ME":"3D6+10","MA":"3D6+12","PS":"3D6+20","PP":"3D6+10","PE":"3D6+12","PB":"2D6+18","Spd":"5D6"}', NULL, NULL, 'PEx70', 'PEx20', 'MEx5', 'Spd base 5D6 gets +10 (water), +24 (Earth), +48 (fire), or +100 (air) depending on element. Hit Points base PEx50 gets +100 (water) or +200 (Earth). P.P.E. is PEx20 +50/level of experience. I.S.P. is MEx5 +12/level. M.D.C. = combined hit points + S.D.C. (given here as the PEx50/PEx20 base sum); add the element-specific hit point bonus above where applicable. Physical attributes apply only when materialized and are supernatural.; In S.D.C. settings: hit points PEx50, S.D.C. PEx20', NULL, 14, '{"attacks":6}', 'Element-specific combat bonuses (on top of attribute bonuses): Air +1 attack/round, +4 initiative, +4 dodge, +2 pull punch, +1 save vs magic, +5 save vs horror factor. Fire +2 attacks/round, +5 initiative, +3 strike, +1 pull punch, +1 save vs magic, +10 save vs horror factor. Water +3 initiative, +1 strike/parry, +2 dodge, +4 pull punch, +1 save vs magic, +5 save vs horror factor. Earth +1 attack/round, +2 initiative, +2 strike, +4 pull punch, +1 save vs magic, +6 save vs horror factor.; damage: As per supernatural P.S. attribute, psionics or magic', 'R.C.C. skills vary by element, all 80%+2%/level: Air gets astronomy/navigation/rogue-type skills, language 96%. Earth gets wilderness/lore skills, language 96%. Fire gets interrogation/dance/lore skills, language 94%. Water gets boating/lore skills, language 92%.', 'Standard spirit traits (energy form, materialization, possession) plus bio-regeneration 1D6x10 M.D.C./minute, fluency in the True Elemental tongue, and 01-80% sensing of hidden spirits/elementals/Shamans within 500 ft.', 'Knows all Warlock spells of its own element; can craft all minor and major fetishes, but sparingly.', 'By element, all with mind block auto-defense: Air - telepathy, empathy, empathic transmission, telekinesis (super), +1D4 sensitive; Fire - telepathy, object read, pyrokinesis, mind bolt, hypnotic suggestion, +1D4 sensitive; Water - telepathy, hydrokinesis, electrokinesis, +1D4+2 healing; Earth - telepathy, bio-manipulation, P.P.E. shield, group mind block, +1D4 physical.', '10 feet (3 m), or the same size as the animal/human form it imitates', 'About 20% more than the normal animal or human it imitates', 'Immortal, but can be destroyed while in energy form', 'Anywhere in North America, especially wilderness and Native American regions', 'Other spirits (lesser and greater); Native American Gods; Native Americans, esp. Pure Ones and Traditionalists; dragons; occasionally alien intelligences', 'Rival forces, gods, and enemies', NULL, 'Elemental guardian spirits of the Kachina; four serve as Standing-Mountain''s lieutenants while others act independently, ranging from benevolent to self-serving.', 'Rifts World Book 15: Spirit West p.147-149');
INSERT INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'ondi-thunderbirds', 'Ondi Thunderbirds', 'spirit', 'rifts', 0, 'Any: 15% scrupulous, 35% unprincipled, 25% anarchist, 10% miscreant, 15% other', '{"IQ":"2D6+5","ME":"2D6+5","MA":"2D6+2","PS":"3D6+26","PP":"2D6+14","PE":"2D6+14","PB":"2D6+14","Spd":"2D6+14"}', NULL, NULL, 'PEx10+3D6x10+18', '3D6x10', '2D6x10', 'Ground speed is 2D6+14; flying speed is a flat 88 (60 mph/96 km/h). Hit points are PEx10 plus 1D6x10 per level of experience. P.P.E. is 3D6x10 plus 30/level. All physical attributes are supernatural.; In S.D.C. settings: hit points PEx10, S.D.C. 3D6x10', NULL, 14, '{"attacks":6,"initiative":5,"strike":2,"parry":2,"dodge":5,"roll":4}', '+1 to save vs magic, +10 to save vs horror factor. Vulnerable to pure iron weapons (which do M.D. instead of S.D.C.; iron rail gun rounds do double damage). Takes half damage from fire and other energy attacks; full damage from magic, magic weapons, missiles and explosions.; damage: As per supernatural P.S. attribute plus claw and bite bonuses', 'Basic Math, land navigation, track animals, track humanoids, sing, intelligence, lore: Indians, lore: demons and monsters, all 80%+2%/level; magically understands all languages at 88%.', 'Sees all light spectrums including infrared/UV, 2-mile nightvision and telescopic vision, bio-regenerates 1D4x10/melee round, needs no air, and is immune to electricity, poison, gas, drugs, disease and fatigue.', 'A handful of spells: blinding flash, globe of daylight, thunderclap, fear, energy disruption, energy bolt, fire bolt, fire ball, fuel flame, and call lightning.', 'Empathy plus six sensitive and two physical psi-powers, and electro-kinesis; I.S.P. 2D6x10.', '20-30 feet (6-9 m) tall; wingspread is twice that', 'Not applicable in energy form', 'Immortal, but destroyed if damage exceeds 100 points below zero while in energy form', 'Highest mountains of North America (esp. the Rockies), the Spirit Realm, and the Astral Plane; most common in the western US, Canada, and Mexico', 'Other Thunderbirds; some Native American Gods; Native Americans, esp. Pure Ones and Traditionalists', 'Enemies of the Thunderbird God; Ukt Water Serpents; Uktena; dragons (mistrusted); evil Shamans; supernatural monsters', NULL, 'Golden lightning-formed eagle spirits that serve as the Thunderbird God''s warriors, striking physically and traveling as living lightning bolts.', 'Rifts World Book 15: Spirit West p.153-154');
INSERT INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'greater-air-spirit', 'Greater Air Spirit', 'spirit', 'rifts', 0, 'Typically good or unprincipled; about 5% anarchist, 2% aberrant, 1% other evil', '{"IQ":"16+1D6","ME":"12+1D4","MA":"16+2D6","PS":"28+2D6","PP":"17+2D6","PE":"20+1D6","PB":"20+2D6","Spd":"50+2D6"}', NULL, NULL, '900', 'PEx20', 'MEx6', 'P.P.E. is PEx20 +25/level; I.S.P. is MEx6 +15/level. Physical attributes apply only when materialized and are supernatural. There are said to be 16 spirits of each element.; In S.D.C. settings: hit points 300, S.D.C. 600', NULL, 15, '{"attacks":5,"initiative":4,"dodge":4,"pull":4}', 'Plus 1 attack per melee round, plus 1 to save vs magic, plus 4 to save vs horror factor; double duration from Temporal magic effects. Horror Factor 15 applies only once its true spirit nature is revealed.; damage: As per supernatural P.S. attribute, psionics or magic', 'All rogue skills except computer hacking, astronomy, navigation, land/basic/advanced math, chemistry, track animals/humanoids, intelligence, surveillance: tailing, detect concealment/ambush, acrobatics, prowl, lore: cattle/animals, lore: Indians, lore: demons/monsters, all 80 percent +2 percent per level; speaks all languages at 98 percent.', 'Knows time/direction and senses wind changes, storms, and airborne contaminants; nightvision 6,000 ft and sees the invisible; unaffected by hurricanes, tornado winds, lightning, cold, disease, and toxins.', 'All Air Warlock spells plus mystic portal; can craft all minor fetishes (major fetishes limited to Great Body and Tattoo types).', 'Telepathy plus all sensitive-category psi-powers, electro-kinesis, telekinesis (super), and telekinetic force field; I.S.P. M.E. x6 plus 15 per level.', 'Varies by form (animal, tree, or human)', 'Varies by form', 'Immortal, but can be destroyed while in energy form', 'Anywhere in North America, especially wilderness and Native American regions', 'Other spirits (lesser and greater); Native American Gods; Native Americans, esp. Pure Ones and Traditionalists', 'Forces of evil; dark spirits; evil Shamans; supernatural monsters; rivals/enemies of Native Americans', NULL, 'One of sixteen legendary air-element nature spirits that can take animal or human form and befriends Elemental Shamans.', 'Rifts World Book 15: Spirit West p.155-157');
INSERT INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'greater-earth-spirit', 'Greater Earth Spirit', 'spirit', 'rifts', 0, 'Typically good or unprincipled; about 5% anarchist, 2% aberrant, 1% other evil', '{"IQ":"14+1D6","ME":"13+2D6","MA":"18+1D6","PS":"35+2D6","PP":"14+1D4","PE":"22+2D4","PB":"16+1D6","Spd":"16+1D6"}', NULL, NULL, '1300+6D6x10', 'PEx20', 'MEx6', 'The plus 6D6x10 extra S.D.C. is specific to Great Earth Elemental Spirits. P.P.E. is PEx20 plus 25 per level; I.S.P. is MEx6 plus 15 per level. Physical attributes apply only when materialized and are supernatural.; In S.D.C. settings: hit points 400, S.D.C. 900+6D6x10', NULL, 15, '{"attacks":5,"initiative":1,"strike":1,"pull":5}', 'Plus 1 attack per melee round, plus 10 to supernatural P.S. damage, plus 1 to save vs magic, plus 5 to save vs horror factor; takes 50 percent more damage from magical water-based attacks. Horror Factor 15 applies only once its true spirit nature is revealed.; damage: As per supernatural P.S. attribute, psionics or magic', 'All wilderness skills, all lore skills, botany, breeding dogs/animals, animal husbandry, basic mathematics, holistic medicine, wilderness survival, climb, all 80 percent plus 2 percent per level; speaks all languages at 90 percent.', 'Identifies minerals on sight, senses seismic disturbances up to 50 plus 10 miles per level and predicts earthquakes/eruptions, senses earth hazards, takes half damage from falls and kinetic attacks, nightvision 6,000 ft; resists cold/heat/disease/toxins and takes half damage from lightning/fire.', 'All Earth Warlock spells plus dimensional portal; can craft all minor fetishes (major fetishes limited to Great Body and Tattoo types).', 'Telepathy plus all physical-category psi-powers, bio-manipulation, P.P.E. shield, psi-shield, and psi-sword; I.S.P. M.E. x6 plus 15 per level.', 'Varies by form (animal, tree, or human)', 'Varies by form', 'Immortal, but can be destroyed while in energy form', 'Anywhere in North America, especially wilderness and Native American regions', 'Other spirits (lesser and greater); Native American Gods; Native Americans, esp. Pure Ones and Traditionalists', 'Forces of evil; dark spirits; evil Shamans; supernatural monsters; rivals/enemies of Native Americans', NULL, 'One of sixteen legendary earth-element nature spirits that can possess soil, stone, or boulders and befriends Elemental Shamans.', 'Rifts World Book 15: Spirit West p.155-157');
INSERT INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'greater-fire-spirit', 'Greater Fire Spirit', 'spirit', 'rifts', 0, 'Typically good or unprincipled; about 5% anarchist, 2% aberrant, 1% other evil', '{"IQ":"13+1D6","ME":"12+1D6","MA":"12+2D6","PS":"22+2D6","PP":"18+1D6","PE":"19+1D4","PB":"16+2D6","Spd":"30+3D6"}', NULL, NULL, '900', 'PEx20', 'MEx6', 'P.P.E. is PEx20 plus 25 per level; I.S.P. is MEx6 plus 15 per level. Physical attributes apply only when materialized and are supernatural.; In S.D.C. settings: hit points 300, S.D.C. 600', NULL, 15, '{"attacks":5,"initiative":5,"strike":2,"pull":1}', 'Plus 2 attacks per melee round, plus 1 to save vs magic, plus 7 to save vs horror factor; takes double damage from magical cold and water-based attacks. Horror Factor 15 applies only once its true spirit nature is revealed.; damage: As per supernatural P.S. attribute, psionics or magic', 'Land navigation, basic mathematics, interrogation, dance, sing, cook, climb, acrobatics, seduction, streetwise, lore: Indians, lore: demons/monsters, all 80 percent plus 2 percent per level; speaks all languages at 90 percent.', 'Estimates temperatures and identifies a fire origin and composition, senses/locates fires up to 50 plus 10 miles per level, sees via infrared/thermo-imaging in smoke to 5,000 ft, tracks by heat; immune to heat/fire/smoke/gas/disease.', 'All Fire Warlock spells plus superior protection circle (with flaming circle and symbols); can craft all minor fetishes (major fetishes limited to Great Body and Tattoo types).', 'Telepathy plus psychic purification, death trance, see aura, pyrokinesis, bio-manipulation, hypnotic suggestion, and mind block auto-defense; I.S.P. M.E. x6 plus 15 per level.', 'Varies by form (animal, tree, or human)', 'Varies by form', 'Immortal, but can be destroyed while in energy form', 'Anywhere in North America, especially wilderness and Native American regions', 'Other spirits (lesser and greater); Native American Gods; Native Americans, esp. Pure Ones and Traditionalists', 'Forces of evil; dark spirits; evil Shamans; supernatural monsters; rivals/enemies of Native Americans', NULL, 'One of sixteen legendary fire-element nature spirits, immune to flame but vulnerable to cold and water, allied with Elemental Shamans.', 'Rifts World Book 15: Spirit West p.155-157');
INSERT INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'greater-water-spirit', 'Greater Water Spirit', 'spirit', 'rifts', 0, 'Typically good or unprincipled; about 5% anarchist, 2% aberrant, 1% other evil', '{"IQ":"15+1D6","ME":"14+2D4","MA":"11+2D6","PS":"24+2D6","PP":"14+1D4","PE":"20+1D6","PB":"18+1D6","Spd":"20+2D6"}', NULL, NULL, '1300', 'PEx20', 'MEx6', 'P.P.E. is PEx20 plus 25 per level; I.S.P. is MEx6 plus 15 per level. Physical attributes apply only when materialized and are supernatural.; In S.D.C. settings: hit points 400, S.D.C. 900', NULL, 15, '{"attacks":5,"initiative":2,"parry":1,"dodge":1,"pull":6}', 'Plus 2 to save vs magic, plus 4 to save vs horror factor; takes double damage from mega-damage attacks and magical fire. Horror Factor 15 applies only once its true spirit nature is revealed.; damage: As per supernatural P.S. attribute, psionics or magic', 'Swim, boat building, pilot sail and row boats, navigation on water, brewing, chemistry (all), all lores, basic and advanced math, all 80 percent plus 2 percent per level; speaks all languages at 94 percent.', 'Knows time via heavens and tides, senses current and tide changes and approaching storms or tidal waves, detects water impurities, dowses at triple range, nightvision 6,000 ft and sees through fog and mist; impervious to ocean depths, tidal waves, lightning, cold, and disease.', 'Water Warlock spells levels 1 through 5 plus close portal; can craft all minor fetishes (major fetishes limited to Great Body and Tattoo types).', 'Telepathy plus all healing-category psi-powers, empathic transmission, mind wipe, and hydro-kinesis; I.S.P. M.E. x6 plus 15 per level.', 'Varies by form (animal, tree, or human)', 'Varies by form', 'Immortal, but can be destroyed while in energy form', 'Anywhere in North America, especially wilderness and Native American regions', 'Other spirits (lesser and greater); Native American Gods; Native Americans, esp. Pure Ones and Traditionalists', 'Forces of evil; dark spirits; evil Shamans; supernatural monsters; rivals/enemies of Native Americans', NULL, 'One of sixteen legendary water-element nature spirits that can possess ponds or stones and befriends Elemental Shamans.', 'Rifts World Book 15: Spirit West p.155-157');
INSERT INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'greater-totem-animal-spirits', 'Greater Totem Animal Spirits', 'spirit', 'rifts', 0, 'Typically good or unprincipled; about 8% anarchist, 4% aberrant, 2% other evil', '{"IQ":"2D6+8","ME":"2D6+10","MA":"2D6+10","PS":"2D6+20","PP":"2D6+12","PE":"2D6+12","PB":"2D6+12","Spd":"2D6+12"}', NULL, NULL, 'PEx1000+2D6x100', '3D6x100', 'MEx3', 'Also gains bonuses from its specific totem animal (see the Totem section). P.P.E. is 3D6x100 plus 100 per level; I.S.P. is MEx3 plus 15 per level. Physical attributes are supernatural when materialized, S.D.C.-based when possessing. Horror Factor typically equals the totem animal H.F. plus 3 (no fixed number given).; In S.D.C. settings: hit points PEx1000, S.D.C. 2D6x100', NULL, NULL, '{"attacks":6,"initiative":4,"strike":1,"parry":1,"dodge":1,"pull":6}', 'Plus 1 to save vs magic, plus 6 to save vs poison and toxins, plus 8 to save vs horror factor; predatory-animal totems get plus 1 attack per melee round; damage from elemental magic sources is doubled.; damage: As per supernatural P.S. attribute', 'All Wilderness and Cowboy skills, all lore, basic math, track humanoids, dance, sing, intelligence, prowl, climb, all 80 percent plus 2 percent per level; speaks all languages at 90 percent.', 'Materializes at roughly twice normal size with its totem species natural abilities doubled in range, damage, and rate, plus nightvision 2,000 ft, plus 50 percent leap, sees the invisible, thermal vision 2,000 ft, shapechanges within its species, and bio-regenerates 1D4x10 M.D.C. per round.', 'Spells levels 1 through 5 plus escape, superior swim as fish, fly as eagle, cure illness, mask of deceit, reduce self, dispel magic barrier, locate, dowsing, purification, familiar link, and 1D4+6 Shamanic spells; crafts lesser and major fetishes, sparingly.', 'All healing and sensitive psi-powers plus Group Mind Block and one extra super psionic ability per two levels; I.S.P. M.E. x3 plus 15 per level.', 'Twice the size of the normal totem animal', 'Twice the weight of the normal totem animal', 'Immortal, but can be destroyed while in energy form', 'Anywhere in North America, especially wilderness and Native American regions', 'Other spirits (lesser and greater); Native American Gods; Native Americans, esp. Pure Ones and Traditionalists', 'Forces of evil; dark spirits; evil Shamans; supernatural monsters; rivals/enemies of Native Americans', NULL, 'Mighty guardian spirits: at birth each Native American receives one as a totem, and they are masters of fetish magic.', 'Rifts World Book 15: Spirit West p.158-159');
INSERT INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'tree-spirits', 'Tree Spirits', 'spirit', 'rifts', 0, 'Typically good or unprincipled; about 4% anarchist, 4% aberrant, 1% other evil', '{"IQ":"2D6+8","ME":"2D6+12","MA":"2D6+8","PS":"3D6+30","PP":"2D6+10","PE":"2D6+20","PB":"3D6+12","Spd":"2D6+8"}', NULL, NULL, 'PEx1000+1D6x1000', '3D6x100', 'MEx10', 'Speed applies in humanoid form. P.P.E. is 3D6x100 plus 100 per level; I.S.P. is MEx10 plus 25 per level. Physical attributes are supernatural when materialized, S.D.C.-based when possessing (a possessed tree is often a light M.D.C. structure: a mature tree has 3D4x100 S.D.C., about 3 to 12 M.D.C.; an ancient tree adds 1D4x1000 S.D.C., about 10 to 40 M.D.C.). Armor Rating runs A.R. 4 for small plants and flowers up to A.R. 10-12 for large trees, depending on the vegetation.; In S.D.C. settings: hit points PEx1000, S.D.C. 1D6x1000', NULL, 14, '{"attacks":4,"initiative":2,"pull":3}', 'Plus 1 to save vs psionics, plus 2 to save vs magic, plus 6 to save vs horror factor; materializing as a tree adds plus 4 attacks and plus 6 parry, possession adds plus 2 attacks and plus 4 parry; fire and electricity do double damage. Horror Factor 14 applies only once its true nature is revealed.; damage: As per supernatural P.S. attribute, psionics or magic', 'All lore, basic math, astronomy, navigation, identify plants and fruits, botany, preserve food, camouflage, carpentry, boat building, whittling/sculpture, trap/mine detection, detect ambush/concealment, wilderness survival, holistic medicine, brewing, cooking, horsemanship, all 80 percent plus 1 percent per level; speaks all languages at 90 percent.', 'Knows time and direction, senses wind and storm changes, identifies minerals, senses seismic disturbances; bio-regenerates 1D4x10 M.D.C. per minute; nightvision 600 ft; resists disease and cold and takes half damage from heat and poison; understands the True Elemental tongue.', 'All Shaman plant spells, Earth elemental spells levels 1 through 3, and conventional spells levels 1 through 4; fetish creation limited to the minor Damage Fetish and major Supernatural Damage Fetish.', 'All healing and sensitive psi-powers plus Group Mind Block and Mind Block Auto-Defense, and cost-free telepathy out to a one mile radius; I.S.P. M.E. x10 plus 25 per level.', 'Varies with the form assumed', 'Varies from pounds to tons depending on the form assumed', 'Immortal, but can be destroyed while in energy form', 'Anywhere in North America, especially wilderness and Native American regions', 'Other spirits (lesser and greater); Native American Gods; Native Americans, esp. Pure Ones and Traditionalists', 'Forces of evil; dark spirits; evil Shamans; supernatural monsters; rivals/enemies of Native Americans', NULL, 'Reclusive forest-guardian spirits that possess or become trees, quietly protecting wilderness domains from destruction and evil.', 'Rifts World Book 15: Spirit West p.159-161');
INSERT INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'nunnehi', 'Nunnehi', 'spirit', 'rifts', 0, 'Typically unprincipled (about 60%); can be good (15%), selfish (15%), or evil (10%)', '{"IQ":"3D6+6","ME":"3D6+10","MA":"3D6+2","PS":"3D6+6","PP":"3D6+6","PE":"2D6+10","PB":"1D6+1","Spd":"3D6+6"}', NULL, NULL, 'PEx100+1D4x1000', 'PEx50', 'MEx10', 'The book heading calls the Nunnehi Considered a Greater Spirit NPC, but its own text says they are not traditional spirits, rather an alien race native to the Spirit Realm and Astral Plane, possibly a naming or classification convention worth reconciling. Gender is neuter (any males or females look identical). Hit points are PEx100 plus 100 per level; P.P.E. is PEx50 plus 30 per level; I.S.P. is MEx10 plus 10 per level. All attributes are supernatural.; In S.D.C. settings: hit points PEx100, S.D.C. 1D4x1000', NULL, 11, '{"attacks":5,"initiative":3,"parry":2,"disarm":2,"pull":4}', 'Plus 3 to save vs magic, plus 7 to save vs horror factor; fire and energy attacks (and all dragon breath types) do double damage; magic other than fire or energy, and psionics, do normal damage.; damage: As per supernatural P.S. attribute', 'All Science, Medical, Wilderness, and lore skills at 78 percent plus 2 percent per level, plus dance, sing, prowl, climb, swim, intelligence, horsemanship: general, wilderness survival, and 1D4 Rogue or Espionage skills at 60 percent plus 2 percent per level; speaks all languages at 90 percent.', 'Sees and turns invisible at will, nightvision 3,000 ft, floats on water, bio-regenerates 1D4x100 per minute and regrows limbs in 24 hours, needs no air or food, resists fatigue, disease, poison, most chemicals, heat, and cold; can teleport itself, enter dreams, and sense possession or true alignment in others.', 'Selects TWO areas of mystic knowledge from: Ley Line Walker spells (levels 1-10 plus 1D6+6 from levels 11-15), Techno-Wizardry, Shifter or Summoning magic, Stone magic, Tattoo magic, Bio-Wizardry, Temporal magic, Herbology, Necromancy, Conjurer magic, or Warlock Earth and Air spells (no O.C.C. abilities); can craft all fetishes.', 'All sensitive abilities plus detect psionics, healing touch, psychic diagnosis, psychic surgery, object read, group mind block, mind block auto-defense, a cost-free natural telepathy, sensing evil supernatural creatures, and seeing into people souls.', '7 to 8 feet (2.1 to 2.4 m) tall', '170 to 220 lbs (76.5 to 99 kg)', 'Immortal, but destroyed if damage exceeds 600 points below zero', 'Anywhere on Earth, most common in North America; also found throughout the Megaverse', 'Other spirits (lesser and greater); many Native American Gods; Native Americans, esp. Pure Ones and Shamans; dragons; Temporal Raiders and Wizards; occasional alien intelligences; Prometheans', 'Supernatural monsters; rivals and enemies of Native Americans', NULL, 'Alien, dimension-traveling humanoids the book files as greater spirits; longtime secret caretakers and magic-rich advisors to Native Americans.', 'Rifts World Book 15: Spirit West p.150-152');

